WEBVTT

00:00:27.791 --> 00:00:32.829
a marriage and family therapist
who has supported clients through loss.

00:00:32.863 --> 00:00:33.997
Hi, Nina.

00:00:34.531 --> 00:00:37.367
Nina Westbrook: Hi, Cloe,
good to see you.

00:00:37.401 --> 00:00:39.336
Thank you so much for having me.

00:00:39.369 --> 00:00:41.104
CSB: Thanks for joining us.

00:00:41.138 --> 00:00:45.208
Nina, you have talked about how grief
can be about the loss of people

00:00:45.242 --> 00:00:46.843
and tangible things.

00:00:46.877 --> 00:00:49.212
But that it can also be
about the loss of dreams,

00:00:49.246 --> 00:00:52.316
something that many people
have experienced over the past year.

00:00:52.849 --> 00:00:55.552
Can you give me some examples
of grieving for lost dreams

00:00:55.586 --> 00:00:58.622
and talk about what it means
to experience this kind of grief?

00:00:59.556 --> 00:01:00.724
NW: Absolutely.